#: source/language/index.md:1
msgid "Nix Language"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:3
msgid ""
"The Nix language is designed for conveniently creating and composing "
"[derivations](../glossary.md#gloss-derivation) – precise descriptions of how "
"contents of existing files are used to derive new files."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:5
msgid "**Tip**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:7
msgid ""
"These pages are written as a reference. If you are learning Nix, nix.dev has "
"a good [introduction to the Nix language](https://nix.dev/tutorials/nix-"
"language)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:10
msgid "The language is:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:12
msgid "_domain-specific_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:14
msgid ""
"The Nix language is purpose-built for working with text files. Its most "
"characteristic features are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:17
msgid ""
"[File system path primitives](../language/types.md#type-path), for accessing "
"source files"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:18
msgid ""
"[Indented strings](../language/string-literals.md) and [string interpolation]"
"(../language/string-interpolation.md), for creating file contents"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:19
msgid ""
"[Strings with contexts](../language/string-context.md), for transparently "
"linking files"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:21
msgid ""
"It comes with [built-in functions](../language/builtins.md) to integrate "
"with the [Nix store](../store/index.md), which manages files and enables "
"[realising](../glossary.md#gloss-realise) derivations declared in the Nix "
"language."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:23
msgid "_declarative_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:25
msgid ""
"There is no notion of executing sequential steps. Dependencies between "
"operations are established only through data."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:28
msgid "_pure_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:30
msgid ""
"Values cannot change during computation. Functions always produce the same "
"output if their input does not change."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:33
msgid "_functional_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:35
msgid ""
"Functions are like any other value. Functions can be assigned to names, "
"taken as arguments, or returned by functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:38
msgid "_lazy_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:40
msgid "Values are only computed when they are needed."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:42
msgid "_dynamically typed_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:44
msgid "Type errors are only detected when expressions are evaluated."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:46
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:48
msgid "This is an incomplete overview of language features, by example."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:63
msgid "_Basic values ([primitives](../language/types.md#primitives))_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:76
msgid "`\"hello world\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:81
msgid "A [string](../language/types.md#type-string)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:100
msgid ""
"A multi-line string. Strips common prefixed whitespace. Evaluates to "
"`\"multi\\n line\\n  string\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:107
msgid "`# Explanation`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:112
msgid "A [comment](../language/syntax.md#comments)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:119
msgid "`\"hello ${ { a = \"world\"; }.a }\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:121
msgid "`\"1 2 ${toString 3}\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:123
msgid "`\"${pkgs.bash}/bin/sh\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:128
msgid ""
"[String interpolation](../language/string-interpolation.md) (expands to "
"`\"hello world\"`, `\"1 2 3\"`, `\"/nix/store/<hash>-bash-<version>/bin/"
"sh\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:135
msgid "`true`, `false`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:140
msgid "[Booleans](../language/types.md#type-bool)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:147
msgid "`null`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:152
msgid "[Null](../language/types.md#type-null) value"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:159
msgid "`123`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:164
msgid "An [integer](../language/types.md#type-int)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:171
msgid "`3.141`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:176
msgid "A [floating point number](../language/types.md#type-float)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:183
msgid "`/etc`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:188
msgid "An absolute [path](../language/types.md#type-path)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:195
msgid "`./foo.png`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:200
msgid ""
"A [path](../language/types.md#type-path) relative to the file containing "
"this Nix expression"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:207
msgid "`~/.config`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:212
msgid ""
"A home [path](../language/types.md#type-path). Evaluates to the `\"<user's "
"home directory>/.config\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:219
msgid "`<nixpkgs>`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:224
msgid ""
"A [lookup path](../language/constructs/lookup-path.md) for Nix files. Value "
"determined by [`$NIX_PATH` environment variable](../command-ref/env-common."
"md#env-NIX_PATH)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:231
msgid "_Compound values_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:243
msgid "`{ x = 1; y = 2; }`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:248
msgid ""
"An [attribute set](../language/types.md#type-attrs) with attributes named "
"`x` and `y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:255
msgid "`{ foo.bar = 1; }`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:260
msgid "A nested set, equivalent to `{ foo = { bar = 1; }; }`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:267
msgid "`rec { x = \"foo\"; y = x + \"bar\"; }`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:272
msgid ""
"A [recursive set](../language/syntax.md#recursive-sets), equivalent to `{ x "
"= \"foo\"; y = \"foobar\"; }`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:279
msgid "`[ \"foo\" \"bar\" \"baz\" ]`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:281
msgid "`[ 1 2 3 ]`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:283
msgid "`[ (f 1) { a = 1; b = 2; } [ \"c\" ] ]`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:288
msgid "[Lists](../language/types.md#type-list) with three elements."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:295
msgid "_Operators_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:307
msgid "`\"foo\" + \"bar\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:312
msgid "String concatenation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:319
msgid "`1 + 2`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:324
msgid "Integer addition"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:331
msgid "`\"foo\" == \"f\" + \"oo\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:336
msgid "Equality test (evaluates to `true`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:343
msgid "`\"foo\" != \"bar\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:348
msgid "Inequality test (evaluates to `true`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:355
msgid "`!true`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:360
msgid "Boolean negation"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:367
msgid "`{ x = 1; y = 2; }.x`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:372
msgid ""
"[Attribute selection](../language/types.md#type-attrs) (evaluates to `1`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:379
msgid "`{ x = 1; y = 2; }.z or 3`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:384
msgid ""
"[Attribute selection](../language/types.md#type-attrs) with default "
"(evaluates to `3`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:391
msgid "`{ x = 1; y = 2; } // { z = 3; }`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:396
msgid "Merge two sets (attributes in the right-hand set taking precedence)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:403
msgid "_Control structures_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:415
msgid "`if 1 + 1 == 2 then \"yes!\" else \"no!\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:420
msgid "[Conditional expression](../language/syntax.md#conditionals)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:427
msgid "`assert 1 + 1 == 2; \"yes!\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:432
msgid ""
"[Assertion](../language/syntax.md#assertions) check (evaluates to `\"yes!"
"\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:439
msgid "`let x = \"foo\"; y = \"bar\"; in x + y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:444
msgid ""
"Variable definition. See [`let`\\-expressions](../language/syntax.md#let-"
"expressions)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:451
msgid "`with builtins; head [ 1 2 3 ]`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:456
msgid "Add all attributes from the given set to the scope (evaluates to `1`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:458
msgid ""
"See [`with`\\-expressions](../language/syntax.md#with-expressions) for "
"details and shadowing caveats."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:465
msgid "`inherit pkgs src;`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:470
msgid ""
"Adds the variables to the current scope (attribute set or `let` binding). "
"Desugars to `pkgs = pkgs; src = src;`. See [Inheriting attributes](../"
"language/syntax.md#inheriting-attributes)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:479
msgid "`inherit (pkgs) lib stdenv;`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:484
msgid ""
"Adds the attributes, from the attribute set in parentheses, to the current "
"scope (attribute set or `let` binding). Desugars to `lib = pkgs.lib; stdenv "
"= pkgs.stdenv;`. See [Inheriting attributes](../language/syntax."
"md#inheriting-attributes)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:493
msgid "_[Functions](../language/syntax.md#functions) (lambdas)_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:505
msgid "`x: x + 1`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:510
msgid ""
"A [function](../language/syntax.md#functions) that expects an integer and "
"returns it increased by 1."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:517
msgid "`x: y: x + y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:522
msgid ""
"Curried [function](../language/syntax.md#functions), equivalent to `x: (y: x "
"+ y)`. Can be used like a function that takes two arguments and returns "
"their sum."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:529
msgid "`(x: x + 1) 100`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:534
msgid "A [function](../language/syntax.md#functions) call (evaluates to 101)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:541
msgid "`let inc = x: x + 1; in inc (inc (inc 100))`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:546
msgid ""
"A [function](../language/syntax.md#functions) bound to a variable and "
"subsequently called by name (evaluates to 103)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:553
msgid "`{ x, y }: x + y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:558
msgid ""
"A [function](../language/syntax.md#functions) that expects a set with "
"required attributes `x` and `y` and concatenates them"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:565
msgid "`{ x, y ? \"bar\" }: x + y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:570
msgid ""
"A [function](../language/syntax.md#functions) that expects a set with "
"required attribute `x` and optional `y`, using `\"bar\"` as default value "
"for `y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:577
msgid "`{ x, y, ... }: x + y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:582
msgid ""
"A [function](../language/syntax.md#functions) that expects a set with "
"required attributes `x` and `y` and ignores any other attributes"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:589
msgid "`{ x, y } @ args: x + y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:591
msgid "`args @ { x, y }: x + y`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:596
msgid ""
"A [function](../language/syntax.md#functions) that expects a set with "
"required attributes `x` and `y`, and binds the whole set to `args`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:603
msgid "_Built-in functions_"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:615
msgid "`import ./foo.nix`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:620
msgid ""
"Load and return Nix expression in given file. See [import](../language/"
"builtins.md#builtins-import)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:628
msgid "`map (x: x + x) [ 1 2 3 ]`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/index.md:633
msgid ""
"Apply a function to every element of a list (evaluates to `[ 2 4 6 ]`). See "
"[`map`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-map)."
msgstr ""
